      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Horizon-scale imaging transformed black holes from theoretical objects into observable astrophysical systems and demonstrated extraordinary long-baseline interferometry.",
        "attribution": "These nominees represent key theoretical, array-building, and observational leadership, though the result depended on a large international collaboration and many observatories.",
        "maturity": "The 2019 image and subsequent observations established a durable result, with continued improvements in resolution and coverage.",
        "uncertainties": [
