        "Claudio Pellegrini",
        "Jörg Rossbach",
        "Tetsuya Ishikawa"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Self-amplified spontaneous emission enabled X-ray free-electron lasers, providing ultrashort, intense coherent pulses that expose matter on atomic and femtosecond scales.",
        "attribution": "Pellegrini contributed foundational accelerator concepts, Rossbach led major facility realization, and Ishikawa led an early operational X-ray FEL; credit spans theory, engineering, and large facilities.",
        "maturity": "Multiple facilities now deliver reliable science, confirming the method's lasting value as an experimental tool.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The nominees' relative contributions across conceptual invention, facility construction, and first scientific operation require careful distinction."
        ]
      }
    }
